              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ANGELLLLLA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This receipe is the BEST dip receipe I've ever made!! EVERYONE WENT NUTS!! My husband say's it's the best dip he's ever eaten and asks for it specifically for parties, etc. It's wonderful!!!\r\nTry campbell's fiesta chili beef soup instead of chili, velveeta mexican (HOT!!)cheese, try adding sausage!!!! YUM!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LINDA MCLEAN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was really good but I arranged the dish a little differently. I mixed softened cream cheese with the salsa and smoothed it into a casserole dish. I then layered with a \"healthy\" chili containing beans (because we love them) to which I added a little cayenne for some heat and again, topped with fresh shredded cheddar and canned chile peppers. I popped the dish into the micorwave for a few minutes and it came out great. Thanks Mary!",
            "datePublished": "2004-03-15T06:43:59.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mmmhmmmgood"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! A real crowd pleaser. It helps to melt the Velveta and the cream cheese in the mivrowave before adding to the sauce pan. Also, it's really good when you add ground beef or sausage!",
            "datePublished": "2009-03-23T10:40:33.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jane Barnett"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this on football Sundays. My husband loves it. It is so easy, I just throw everything into a crock pot about an hour in advance and it's ready to go.\nI always get complements on it.",
            "datePublished": "2008-09-28T18:12:03.683Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jbundles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "YUMM- my family loved this! Made it on the stove top and then transferred to a mini dip crock pot. Used medium salsa but regular velveeta (lots of kids here) and hormel chili with no beans (although beans would have been fine). I did add about an ounce more velveeta bc I like it cheesy (or in this case- fake cheesy!). Everyone ate it up- will make again for another football party! I searched through so many recipes and this was perfect for what I was looking for. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2007-01-21T20:56:00.373Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christina"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for our 'dip night' last night and we LOVED it! I did use chili with beans because we like it, but made no other changes otherwise. I just popped everything into my mini slow cooker and let it go, stirring occasionally, until it was all melted and combined. This was super tasty and a definate keeper in my house! Thanks for sharing. :)",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-08T03:41:06.610Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HMILANO"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As suggested by other members, I used Velveeta Jalapeno Cheese, The Campbells Chili Soup, and hot sausage and it completely made this dip. I am not sure how delicious it would have been without these specifics. Took to a party where it was a hit! Making it for another party tonight...it was super when it was hot, but yet still great cold! Never going back to old Taco dip!",
            "datePublished": "2003-12-20T06:48:15.380Z"
          },
